####Information for the site data######

A generic namelist to run SiB4 is in the namel_sibdrv file.
A list of all the sites is in the site_infolist.xlsx file.
A list of sites specific to PFTs is in the site_pftlist.txt file.  
  --These are the sites used for testing and development.

Site Data for SiB4 Simulations are available at:
http://bit.ly/2KPLtEI

#########Required for each site simulation########
1) namel_sibdrv

   -Namelist file to run SiB4, specified with site info/files
   -You will need to replace the XX-XXX placeholders with the
    name of the site you are simulating.

   -Information on all of the variables listed in the file
    is found at the bottom of the namel_sibdrv file
   -Namelist variables you may need to modify:
      --CONTROL_LIST_SIBDRV, simulations options
        (nsib, starttime, startyear, endtime, endyear,
         dtsib, dtsibrestart, dtsibqp, dtsibpbp, dtsibhr)

      --IO_LIST_SIBDRV, input files and output locations
        (parameter files, input files, output directories)

      --SPINUP_LIST_SIBDRV, spinup options
        (spinup, spinup_default, spinup_output, spinup_numyrs, 
         spinup_maxiter, spinup_threshold)

      --SUBGRID_SIBDRV, subgrid lat/lon specifications if desired
        (minlon, maxlon, minlat, maxlat)

      --PBP_LIST_SIBDRV, specific points to save psib data at
        (npbp, list of points) (npbp = -1 ==> all points)

      --BALAN_LIST_SIBDRV, water and energy balance information
        (flags and thresholds for balances)
 
      --PRINT_LIST_SIBDRV, screen-printing options during simulation

      --SWITCH_LIST_SIBDRV, specific model options/switches
        (cornsoy, fire, grazing, green, equibclear, leapyear, updatelst)
 

2) sib_vs.txt

    -Vegetation structure file
    -Set to the PFT defined at the site
   
    -To create: use the fortran program in
          sib4_corral/tools_pre/make_subdomain_sibvs.f90
     This pulls out the PFT information from a global file.

     Modify the information file make_subdomain.txt
     --For a single site, set the subdomain type to 1.
     --For specific sites, you may need to modify the PFTs included
         to match the site descriptions.  Options are now available
         to set a specific PFT or use the default in the global file 
         (specific PFT in input file==PFT number or -1 for default)
     --Specify the output location

3) driver data ==> MERRA

  -MERRA driver data for the site

  -To create these data, use the program in
       sib4_corral/tools_pre/make_subdomain_sibdr_new.f90
   This program pulls the site information
        from global driver data (typically MERRA).

   Modify the information file make_subdomain.txt
    >Check the input driver directory
     (typically '/archive/MERRA2_0.5x0.5/merra2_0.5deg_')
    >Check the output location 
     (adds on the merra subdirectory and "merra2_" prefix)
    >Check the starting year, stopping year, and output type
      (typically for single sites, the output type should be 1)
    >Set the number of sites desired
    >Specify the lat/lon/site name of the desired new sites

4) fire data ==> GFED v4

   -To create these data, use the program
       sib4_corral/tools_pre/make_subdomain_sibfire.f90
    This program pulls the site information
         from global fire emissions.

     Modify the information file make_subdomain.txt
       >Check the input fire directory
       >Check the output location
         (adds on the site and gfed4 subdirectory,
	   along with "gfed4_" prefix)
       >Check starting year, stopping year, and output type
         (typically for single sites, the output type should be 1)
	 (GFED only available 2003-2018)
       >Set the number of sites desired
       >Specify the lat/lon/site name of the sites

Those files should be all the site-specific files necessary for a 
site simulation.
   

#######To perform a site simulation#########
1) Make sure you have the latest version of SiB4
    --> If you don't yet have SiB4, 
         use git to check it out:
        -Type: git clone https://USERNAME@gitlab.com/kdhaynes/sib4v2_corral.git
        -This will download the SiB4 code and all the 
          additional information/tools
        -By default, this will create a folder called
           'sib4v2_corral'
    --> If you already have SiB4, use git to 
        make sure you have the latest version:
        -Type: 'git pull'

2) Compile SiB4
   -In the sib4_corral/code directory, type 'make'
   -Move the executable to the main directory 
     (mv SiB4D ..)

3) Copy the namel_sibdrv file, with edits for the 
   specific site, to the main directory with the 
   executable
   -- Sample namel_sibdrv files are in 
      sib4_corral/info/sites/namel_sibdrv (for sites)
      sib4_corral/info/groups/namel_sibdrv (for groups)
      sib4_corral/info/global/namel_sibdrv (for global)
   -- Check the input files, output directory, 
      time period, and output file frequency 

4) Specify any specific variables to output in the
   sib4_corral/input/sib_outopts file
   - This file controls all the output in SiB4, 
      with each column containing a flag of whether or
      not to include the variable in the output 
      (T=output, F=no output)
   - The first column if for the qp files (typically monthly)
   - The second column is for the pbp files (typically daily)
   - The third column is for the hr files (typically hourly)

5) Perform a spin-up simulation to get equilibrium pools
   - In the namel_sibdrv file, make sure "spinup == .true."
   - Model output is typically not produced during spin-up runs, 
      unless in the namel_sibdrv file you set spinup_output=.true.
   - In the main directory, type: './SiB4D >sib4.out'
   - Check the equilibrium pools in the standard output
      saved in the sib4.out file
   
6) Save the equilibrium pool restart file produced from
   the spin-up simulation.
   - Rename the final spinup restart file as sib_requib.nc
   - Move the restart file to a directory set-up for the site
      i.e. username/sib4_driver/sites/xx-xxx/sib_requib.nc

7) Change the namel_sibdrv file for a regular simulation
   (ic_path == /xxx/sib_requib.nc; spinup == .false.)

8) Perform the simulation (type './SiB4D')
    - Run with no command-line variables (as above)
      to use the namel_sibdrv folder found in the same
      directory as the executable, typically in 
      the sib4_corral directory
    - Run with a single command-line variable 
      specifying a specific namel_sibdrv to use
      (i.e. typing './SiB4D ./sample/namel_sibdrv'
       will run with the namel_sibdrv in the specified
       directory)
    - Run with two integer command-line variables to
      perform multiple simulations in parallel 
      (typically for global runs).  The first is
      the rank you wish to perform and the second
      is the total number of different simulations.
      For example, to divide the simulation into 
      three smaller simulations you'd need to start 
      three runs: 'SiB4D 1 3', 'SiB4D 2 3', SiB4D 3 3'
    

#######Basic Steps for Re-Running Sites############
Once you follow the full procedure and have the restart file
with equilibrium pools, you do only have to redo the spin-up
simulation for:
  - Changes to the parameter files 
     (in sib4_corral/input/params/)
  - Changes to the code that would affect the long-term
     pool sizes (i.e. roots/wood/soil)

Otherwise, to rerun a site once you have all the input
data setup:
1) Make sure you have the latest SiB4
2) If changes have been made to any file in the 
   sib4_corral/code directory, you will need to recompile
   and then move the executable to the trunk directory
3) Make sure you have the namelist and output options correct
4) Re-run


#######Output Viewing/Analysis Options############
1) sib4plot
   - IDL program included in the sib4_corral/sib4plot folder,
     with a README for set-up
   - In IDL, type 'sib4plot', which opens the program
   - Capable of opening all the model output, 
     as well as the input data and generic netcdf files
   - Performs simple comparisons and analysis  
   - Allows the data to be easily viewed
     and creates plots that can be easily saved

2) Combine or edit the output files using the fortran 
    programs in the sib4_corral/tool_post directory


